{
  "title": "9: al-Tawbah التوبة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بَرَآءَةٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ؕ‏(1)\nBARAAATUN MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI ELAL LAZEENA A’AAHADTTUM MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\n(This a declaration of) Immunity from God and His Apostle (Muhammad) towards those of the idolaters with whom ye have (mutually) covenanted.\nفَسِيْحُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ اَرْبَعَةَ اَشْهُرٍ وَّاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِى اللّٰهِۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْزِى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(2)\nFASEEHOOA FIL ARZE ARBA-A’TA ASH-HORINW WWAAA’LAMOOA ANNAKUM GHAYRO MUA’JEZEAA LAAHE WA ANNAL LAAHA MUKHZEAA KAAFEREEN.\nSo go ye about in the earth for four months, and know ye that ye are not weakening God, and that God bringeth shame unto the infidels.\nوَاَذَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَى النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْحَجِّ الْاَكْبَرِ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ بَرِىْۤءٌ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ۙ  وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ ؕ فَاِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍۙ‏(3)\nWAAZAANUN MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI ELAL NAASE YAWMA HAJJE WA AL-AAKBARE ANNAL LAAHA BAREAAUN MENAL MUSHREKEEN WA RASOOLUH FA-IN IN TUBTUM FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM WA TAWALLAYTUM FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAKUM GHAYRO MUA’JEZEAA LAAHE WA BASH-SHERIL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-A’ZAABIN A’ZAABAN LEEMIN.\nAnd an Announcement from God and His Apostle unto the people on the day of the great pilgrimage, that God is immune (from any obligation to) the idolaters, and (so is) His Apostle; therefore if ye repent, better will it be for you, and if ye turn back, then know ye that ye are not weakening God; and announce thou (O’ Our Apostle!) unto those who dis-believe, a painful chastisement.\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْقُصُوْكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَمْ يُظَاهِرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ اَحَدًا فَاَتِمُّوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ عَهْدَهُمْ اِلٰى مُدَّتِهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(4)\nILLAA LAZEENA A’AAHADTTUM MENAL MUSHREKEEN SUMMA LAM YANQUSOOKUM SHAY-ANW LAM YUZAAHEROOA A’LAYKUM AHADAN FAATEMMOOA ELAYHIM A’AHDAHUM ELAA MUDDATEHEM INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nExcept those (with whom) ye have entered into a pact, from the Idolaters who thereafter failed not you in aught and have backed not any one against you, then fulfil their pact unto the end of their term; Verily God loveth those who guard themselves (against evil).\nفَاِذَا انْسَلَخَ الْاَشْهُرُ الْحُرُمُ فَاقْتُلُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُّمُوْهُمْ وَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاحْصُرُوْهُمْ وَاقْعُدُوْا لَهُمْ كُلَّ مَرْصَدٍ ۚ فَاِنْ تَابُوْا وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ فَخَلُّوْا سَبِيْلَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(5)\nFA-EZAA ANSALAKHA AL-AASHHURU AL-HURUMU FAAQTULOOA MUSHREKEEN HAYSO WAJADTTUMOOHUM WAKHUZOOHUM WAAHSUROOHUM WAAQU’UDOOA LAHUM KULLA MARSADIN FA-IN TAABOO WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA AAATAWUA ZAKAATA FAKHALLOOA SABEELAHUM INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nSo when the sacred months are past then slay the idolaters wherever ye find them, and seize them and besiege them and lie in wait for them in every ambush, then if they repent and establish prayer, and give the poor-rate, then leave their way free to them; Verily God is the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nوَاِنْ اَحَدٌ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اسْتَجَارَكَ فَاَجِرْهُ حَتّٰى يَسْمَعَ كَلَامَ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ اَبْلِغْهُ مَاْمَنَهٗ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA AHAD MENAL MUSHREKEEN ASTAJAARAKA FAAJERHU HATTAA YASMAA’A KALAAMAL LAAHE SUMMA AABLEGHHU MAAMANAH ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUN LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd if anyone from the idolaters seeketh protection from thee, grant thou protection to him till he hears the Word of God, then convey him to his place of safety; This because they are a people who know not.\nكَيْفَ يَكُوْنُ لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ عَهْدٌ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ رَسُوْلِهٖۤ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ عَاهَدتُّمْ عِنْدَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ فَمَا اسْتَقَامُوْا لَكُمْ فَاسْتَقِيْمُوْا لَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(7)\nKAYFA LAHUL LIL-MUSHREKEENA A’AHDUN I’NDAL LAAHE WA I’NDAL RASOOLEHI ILLAA LAZEENA A’AAHADTTUM I’NDAL MASJEDIL HARAAME FAMAA TATANAZZALO LAKUM FASTAQEEMOO LAHUM INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nHow can there be a covenant for the idolaters with God and with His Apostle except (for) those with whom ye made a covenant at the Sacred Mosque? So long as they stand faithful to you, then be ye too faithful to them; Verily God loveth those who guard themselves (against evil).\nكَيْفَ وَاِنْ يَّظْهَرُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ لَا يَرْقُبُوْا فِيْكُمْ اِلًّا وَّلَا ذِمَّةً ؕ يُرْضُوْنَكُمْ بِاَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَتَاْبٰى قُلُوْبُهُمْۚ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَۚ‏(8)\nKAYFA WA YYAZHAROOA A’LAYKUM LAA YARQUBOOA FEEKUM AELLAN WA LAA ZEMMATAN YURZOONAKUM BE-AFWAA-HEHIM WATAABAA QULOOBUHUM WA AKSAROHUM FAASEQOONA.\nHow (can there be any alliance!) while they overcome you they regard not in you any tie nor of any covenant; They allure you with (the sweet words of) their mouths while their hearts are averse (from you), and most of them are transgressors.\nاِشْتَرَوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا فَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(9)\nAESHTARAWA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE SAMANAN QALEELAA FA-SADDU A’N SABEELEH INNAHUM SAAA-A MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThey have bartered the signs of God for a small price, so they turn others away from His way; Verily evil is what they do.\nلَا يَرْقُبُوْنَ فِىْ مُؤْمِنٍ اِلًّا وَّلَا ذِمَّةً ؕ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُعْتَدُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAA YARQUBOONA FEE MUMENIN AELLAN WA LAA ZEMMATAN WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL AL-MUA’TADOONA.\nThey pay not regard in the case of a believer, to any tie nor to any covenant; and these are they who transgress the limits.\nفَاِنْ تَابُوْا وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ فَاِخْوَانُكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِؕ وَنُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(11)\nFA-IN TAABOO WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATA FA-IKHWAANOKUM FIL DEEN WA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nBut if repent they and establish regular prayer and give away the regular charity, then they are your brethren in faith; and We explain the signs for the people who know.\nوَاِنْ نَّكَثُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ عَهْدِهِمْ وَطَعَنُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْ فَقَاتِلُوْۤا اَئِمَّةَ الْكُفْرِۙ اِنَّهُمْ لَاۤ اَيْمَانَ لَهُمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَنْتَهُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA NNAKASOOA AYMAANAHUM MIN BA’DE A’AHDEHEM WATAA’ANOOA FEE DEENEKUM FAQAATELOOA AAEMMATA AL-KUFRE INNAHUM LAA AAYMAANA LAHUM LA-A’LLAHUM YANTAHOONA.\nAnd if they violate their oaths after their covenant and revile your religion, then fight the leaders of infidelity, Verily there is no oath for them, so that they may desist.\nاَلَا تُقَاتِلُوْنَ قَوْمًا نَّكَثُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ وَهَمُّوْا بِاِخْرَاجِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَهُمْ بَدَءُوْكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ؕ اَتَخْشَوْنَهُمْ ۚ فَاللّٰهُ اَحَقُّ اَنْ تَخْشَوْهُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(13)\nALAA TUQAATELOONA QAWMAN NNAKASOOA AYMAANAHUM WAHAMMOOA BEAEKHRAAJE RASOOLE WA HUM BADAOOKUM AWWALA MARRAH AATAKHSHAWNAHUM FAL-LAAHO AHAQQO AN TAKHSHAWHU IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nWhat! will ye not fight the people who violated their oaths and aimed at the expulsion of the Apostle, and they attacked you first; What! do ye fear them? whereas God is the most deserving that ye should fear Him, if ye are believers.\nقَاتِلُوْهُمْ يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِاَيْدِيْكُمْ وَيُخْزِهِمْ وَيَنْصُرْكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَيَشْفِ صُدُوْرَ قَوْمٍ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(14)\nQAATELOOHUM YUA’AZZEBHUMU LAAHO BE-AYDEEKUM WAYUKHZEHEM WAYANSURKUM A’LAYHIM WAYASHFE SUDOORA QAWMIN MOAMENEEN.\nFight them, that God may chastise them by your hands and put them to shame, and help you (to victory) over them and heal the (injured) breast of a believer people.\nوَيُذْهِبْ غَيْظَ قُلُوْبِهِمْ ؕ وَ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(15)\nWAYUZHEB GHAYZA QOLOOBEHIM WA YATOOBU LAAHO A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd removeth He the rage of the hearts; And God turneth (merciful) unto whomsoever He pleaseth; and Verily God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nاَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ اَنْ تُتْرَكُوْا وَلَمَّا يَعْلَمِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ جَاهَدُوْا مِنْكُمْ وَلَمْ يَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا رَسُوْلِهٖ وَلَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَلِيْجَةً ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nAM HASIBTUM AN TUTRAKOOA WA LAMMAA YAA’LAME LAAHO LAZEENA JAAHADOO MINKUM WA LAM YATTAKHEZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAA RASOOLEHI WA LAA MOAMENEEN WALEEJATAN WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nOr think ye (O’ believers!) that ye will be left away while God yet knoweth not those of you who strove and did not take any one as an intervener besides God, and His Apostle and the believers, And verily God is fully aware of what all ye do.\nمَا كَانَ لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اَنْ يَّعْمُرُوْا مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ شٰهِدِيْنَ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ بِالكُفْرِؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ ۖۚ وَ فِى النَّارِ هُمْ خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(17)\nMAA KAANA LIL-MUSHREKEENA AN YYAA’MUROOA MANA-A’ LAAHE SHAAHEDEENA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM BEALKUFRE AOOLAAEKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM WA FIL NAAR HUM KHAALEDOON.\nIt is not for the idolaters to maintain the Mosques of God, themselves bearing witness upon their (own) selves against (their) infidelity; These it is (whose) deeds are made in vain, and in the fire (of Hell) shall they abide.\nاِنَّمَا يَعْمُرُ مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَاَ قَامَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَى الزَّكٰوةَ وَلَمْ يَخْشَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ فَعَسٰٓى اُولٰۤئِكَ اَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مِنَ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(18)\nINNAMAA YAA’MURU MANA-A’ LAAHE MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA QAAMA SALAATA WA AATAZ ZAKAATA WA LAM YAKHSHA ILLAA LAAHA FA-A’SAA AOOLAAEKA AN YYAKOONOOA MENAL AL-MUHTADEENA.\nOnly he shall maintain the Mosques of God who believeth in God and the Last Day, (of requital) and established prayer and giveth away the poor-rate and feareth not (anyone) but God; so these, it may be that they are of the rightly guided ones.\nاَجَعَلْتُمْ سِقَايَةَ الْحَآجِّ وَعِمَارَةَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ كَمَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَجَاهَدَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ لَا يَسْتَوٗنَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۘ‏(19)\nAAJAA’ALTUM SEQAAYATA AL-HAAJJE WAE’EMAARATA MASJEDIL HARAAME KAMAM AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA JAAHADA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAA YASTAWNA I’NDAL LAAHE WA LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nWhat! make ye the giving of drink to the pilgrims and maintenance of the Sacred Mosque, equal to the one who believeth in God and the Last Day, (of requital) and striveth in God’s way? They are not equal in God’s view; and verily God guideth not the unjust people.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ هَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْۙ اَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً عِنْدَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(20)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM AAA’ZAMU DARAJATAN I’NDAL LAAH WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\nThose who believed (in God), and migrated and strove in God’s way with their properties and their selves are the highest in rank in God’s view; and those and they (only) are the achievers (of salvation).\nيُبَشِّرُهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنْهُ وَرِضْوَانٍ وَّجَنّٰتٍ لَّهُمْ فِيْهَا نَعِيْمٌ مُّقِيْمٌ ۙ‏(21)\nYUBASSHERUHUM RABBOHUM BERAHMATIN MINHO WAREZWAANIN WA LAHUM FEEHAA NAE’EEMUN MMUQEEMUN.\nGiveth glad tidings unto them their Lord, of mercy from Him and (His) pleasure and of gardens wherein for them are lasting bounties (from their Lord).\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗۤ اَجْرٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(22)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM INNAL LAAHA I’NDAHU AJRUN A’ZEEM.\n(of) Abiding therein for ever; Verily God, with Him is a great reward.\nيٰۤاَ يُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوْۤا اٰبَآءَكُمْ وَاِخْوَانَكُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ اِنِ اسْتَحَبُّوا الْكُفْرَ عَلَى الْاِيْمَانِ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَوَلَّهُمْ مِّنْكُمْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(23)\nYAA A’ZAABAN AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA AABAAA-AKUM WAAKHWAANAKUM AAWLEEAAAA ENIS ASTAHABBOOA KUFRA A’LAL AL-AEEMAANE WA MAN YYATAWALLAHUM MINKUM FAAWLAAEKA HOMUL ZAALEMOON.\nO’ ye who believe! take ye not your fathers and brothers for friends if they love infidelity above (more than) faith; and whosoever of you make friends of them, then these it is who are the unjust.\nقُلْ اِنْ كَانَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ وَاَبْنَآؤُكُمْ وَاِخْوَانُكُمْ وَاَزْوَاجُكُمْ وَعَشِيْرَتُكُمْ وَ اَمْوَالُ ۨاقْتَرَفْتُمُوْهَا وَتِجَارَةٌ تَخْشَوْنَ كَسَادَهَا وَ مَسٰكِنُ تَرْضَوْنَهَاۤ اَحَبَّ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَ جِهَادٍ فِىْ سَبِيْلِهٖ فَتَرَ بَّصُوْا حَتّٰى يَاْتِىَ اللّٰهُ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(24)\nQUL IN KAANA AAABAAUKUM WAABNAAUKUM WAAKHWAANUKUM WAAZWAAJUKUM WAA’ASHEERATUKUM WA AAMWAALU AQTARAFTUMOOHAA WATEJAARATUN TAKHSHAWNA KASAADAHAA WA MASAAKENU TARZAWNAHAA AAHABBA ELAYKUM MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA JEHAADIN FEE SABEELEH FA TARA BBASOOA HATTAA HATTAA LAAHO LAAHO WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ FAASEQEEN.\nSay; (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “If your fathers, and your sons and your brethren and your mates or your kindred, and properties which ye have acquired, and trade the dullness of which ye fear, and the dwellings which ye delight with, be dearer to you than God and His Apostle and striving in His way, then wait ye until God bringeth about His command; And verily God guideth not the transgressing people.\nلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيْرَةٍ ۙ وَّيَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ ۙ اِذْ اَعْجَبَتْكُمْ كَثْرَتُكُمْ فَلَمْ تُغْنِ عَنْكُمْ شَيْئًا وَّضَاقَتْ عَلَيْكُمُ الْاَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ ثُمَّ وَلَّيْتُمْ مُّدْبِرِيْنَۚ‏(25)\nLAQAD NASARAKUMU LAAHO FEE MAWAATENA KASEERATIL WWAYAWMA HUNAYNIN IZ A-A’JABATKUM KASRATUKUM FALAM TUGHNE A’NKUM SHAY-ANW WWAZAAQAT A’LAYKOMUL ARZO BEMAA RAHUBAT SUMMA WALLAYTUM MMUDBEREENA.\nMost certainly did God help you in many (battle) fields, and on the day of Hunayn, when made you vain your great numbers, but they availed you nothing, and was straitened the earth against you with all its extensiveness, then ye turned back in retreat.\nثُمَّ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ سَكِيْنَتَهٗ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَاَنْزَلَ جُنُوْدًا لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا ۚ وَعَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(26)\nSUMMA ANZALAL LAAHO SAKEENATAHU A’LAA RASOOLEHI WA MOAMENEEN WA ANZALA JUNOODAN LAM TARAWHAA WAA’AZZABA LAZEENA KAFAROO WAZAA LEKA JAZAAA-O KAAFEREEN.\nThen did send down God His tranquillity upon His Apostle and upon the believers, and did send down hosts which ye did not see, and chastised those who disbelieved; and that is the recompense of the infidels.\nثُمَّ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰ لِكَ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(27)\nSUMMA YATOOBU LAAHO MIN BA’DE ZAA LEKA A’LAA MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThen will God turn merciful after this to whomsoever He willeth; and verily God is the Oft-Forgiving, the All-Merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّمَا الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ نَجَسٌ فَلَا يَقْرَبُوا الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ بَعْدَ عَامِهِمْ هٰذَا ۚ وَ اِنْ خِفْتُمْ عَيْلَةً فَسَوْفَ يُغْنِيْكُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖۤ اِنْ شَآءَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(28)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAMAA AL-MUSHREKOONA NAJASUN FALAA YAQRABOOA MASJEDIL HARAAMA BA’DA A’AAMEHEM HAAZAA WA IN KHIFTUM A’AYLATAN FA-SAWFA YUGHNEEKUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI IN SHAAA-AL INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! Verily, Verily the idolaters are unclean, so they shall approach not the Sacred Mosque after this their year; and if ye fear poverty, then soon will God enrich you through His grace if He willed; Verily God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nقَاتِلُوا الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَلَا بِالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَلَا يُحَرِّمُوْنَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗ وَلَا يَدِيْنُوْنَ دِيْنَ الْحَقِّ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ حَتّٰى يُعْطُوا الْجِزْيَةَ عَنْ يَّدٍ وَّهُمْ صٰغِرُوْنَ‏(29)\nQAATELOOA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA BE-YAWME AAKHERE WA LAA YUHARREMOONA MAA HARRAMA LAAHO WA RASOOLUH WA LAA YADEENOONA DEENA HAQQE MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA HATTAA YUA’TOOA AL-JEZYATA A’N YYADIN WA HUM SAAGHEROON.\nFight ye those who believe not in God, and nor in the Last Day, and nor do they prohibit what God and His Apostle have prohibited, nor follow the religion of truth, of those who have been given the Book, until they pay the (‘Jizya’) Tributory tax with their hand and they remain subjected.\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ عُزَيْرُ ۨابْنُ اللّٰهِ وَقَالَتِ النَّصٰرَى الْمَسِيْحُ ابْنُ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰ لِكَ قَوْلُهُمْ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ ۚ يُضَاهِئُونَ قَوْلَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ اَنّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏‏(30)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO U’UZAYRU ABNU LAAHE WA QAALATIL AN-NASAARAA AL-MASEEHU ABNU LAAH ZAA LEKA QAWLOHUM BE-AFWAAHEKUM FWAAHEHEM YUZAAHEOONA QAWLA LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QABLO QAATALAHUMU LAAHO ANNAA YOAFEKOON.\nAnd say the Jews: “Ezra is the son of God;” and say the Christians: “Messiah is the son of God;” These are the words of their mouths; (In this) they (only) imitate the saying of those who disbelieved before; God fighteth them; How they turn away!\nاِتَّخَذُوْۤا اَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ اَرْبَابًا مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَسِيْحَ ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ ۚ وَمَاۤ اُمِرُوْۤا اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلٰهًا وَّاحِدًا ۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(31)\nITTAKHAZOO AAHBAARAHUM WARUHBAANAHUM AARBAABAN MIN DOONIL LAAHE WAL MASEEHA NA MARYAMAL WA MAA MAAA OMEROO ILLAA LEEA’BUDOOA ELAAHANW WAAHEDANW LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA WALADAN A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nTake they their divines and monks as (their) lords besides God, and (also) Messiah son of Mary while they were not commanded but that they (should) worship God the Only One; There is no god but He; Pure is He and Exalted is He from what they associate (with Him).\nيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يُّطْفِئُوْا نُوْرَ اللّٰهِ بِاَ فْوَاهِهِمْ وَيَاْبَى اللّٰهُ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّتِمَّ نُوْرَهٗ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(32)\nYOREEDOONA AN YYUTFEOOA NOORA LAAHE BE-AFWAAHEKUM FWAAHEHEM WAYAABAA LAAHO ILLAA AN YOTIMMAR NOORAH WA LAW KAREHA KAAFEROON.\nIntend they that they put out the Light of God with (the blow of) their mouths, and disdaineth God save that He perfecteth His Light, though may detest it the infidels.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ رَسُوْلَهٗ بِالْهُدٰى وَدِيْنِ الْحَقِّ لِيُظْهِرَهٗ عَلَى الدِّيْنِ كُلِّهٖۙ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\nHOWA LAZEE ARSALA RASOOLAHU BIL-HODAA WA DEENIL HAQQE LE-YUZHERAHU A’LAL DEENE KULLEH WA LAW KAREHA AL-MUSHREKOONA.\nHe it is Who sent His Apostle with guidance and the religion of truth, that He may prevail it over all other religions, though may detest it the polytheists.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الْاَحْبَارِ وَالرُّهْبَانِ لَيَاْكُلُوْنَ اَمْوَالَ النَّاسِ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَكْنِزُوْنَ الذَّهَبَ وَالْفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَهَا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِۙ فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ اَلِيْمٍۙ‏(34)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL KASEERAA MENAL AL-AAHBAARE WAALRRUHBAANE LAYAAKULOONA AAMWAALA NAASE BIL-BAATELE WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAH WAL LAZEENA YAKNEZOONA AZ-ZAHABA WAL FEZZATA WA LAA YUNFEQOONAHAA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA-BASH-SHIRHUM BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! verily many of the divines and the monks eat away the properties of men falsely, and obstruct (others) from the way of God; and those who hoard up gold and silver and spend it not in God’s way; announce thou unto them a painful chastisement.\nيَّومَ يُحْمٰى عَلَيْهَا فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ فَتُكْوٰى بِهَا جِبَاهُهُمْ وَجُنُوْبُهُمْ وَظُهُوْرُهُمْؕ هٰذَا مَا كَنَزْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْ فَذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْنِزُوْنَ‏(35)\nYYAWMA YUHMAA A’LAYHAA FEE NAARE JAHANNAMA FATUKWAA BEHAA JEBAAHUHUM WAJUNOOBUHUM WAZUHOORUHUM HAAZAA MAA KANAZTUM MAA TOQADDEMOO FA-ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TAKNEZOONA.\nOn the Day (of Judgment) when it shall be heated in the fire of hell, then shall be branded with it their foreheads and their sides and their backs; (saying unto them) “This is what ye hoarded up for your selves, taste ye then what ye did hoard up.\nاِنَّ عِدَّةَ الشُّهُوْرِ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ اثْنَا عَشَرَ شَهْرًا فِىْ كِتٰبِ اللّٰهِ يَوْمَ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ مِنْهَاۤ اَرْبَعَةٌ حُرُمٌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الدِّيْنُ الْقَيِّمُ ۙ فَلَا تَظْلِمُوْا فِيْهِنَّ اَنْفُسَكُمْ ؕ وَقَاتِلُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ كَآفَّةً كَمَا يُقَاتِلُوْنَكُمْ كَآفَّةً  ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(36)\nINNAL E’EDDATA ASH-SHUHOORE I’NDAL LAAHE ASNAA A’ASHARA SHAHRAN FEE KETAABIL LAAHE YAWMA KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA MINHAA AARBAA’ATUN HURUMUN ZAA LEKA DEENO AL-QAYMU FALAA TAZLEMOOA FEEHINNA ANFOSAKUM WAQAATELOOA MUSHREKEEN KAAAF-FATANW KAMAA YOQAATELOONAKUM KAAAF-FATANW WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nVerily the number of months with God is twelve months in God’s Book, (since) the Day He created the heavens and the earth; of these (months) four are sacred; that is the established religion, so be ye not unjust therein unto your selves, and fight ye the polytheists all together, even as they fight you all together; and know ye that God is with the pious ones.\nاِنَّمَا النَّسِىْٓءُ زِيَادَةٌ فِى الْكُفْرِ يُضَلُّ بِهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُحِلُّوْنَهٗ عَامًا وَّيُحَرِّمُوْنَهٗ عَامًا لِّيُوَاطِئُوْا عِدَّةَ مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ فَيُحِلُّوْا مَا حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ ؕ زُيِّنَ لَهُمْ سُوْۤءُ اَعْمَالِهِمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(37)\nINNAMAA AN-NASEAAAAU ZEEADATUN FIL AL-KUFRE YUZALLU BEHIL LAZEENA KAFAROO YUHELLOONAH A’AMAA WWAYUHARREMOONAH A’AMAA LLEEWAATEOOA E’EDDATA MAA HARRAMA LAAHO FAYUHELLOOA MAA HARRAMA LAAHO ZUYYENA LAHUM SOOU AAA’MAALEHEM WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ KAAFEREEN.\nVerily the postponing (of the sacred month) is only an addition unto infidelity, with which those who disbelieve get astray, they allow it one year and forbid it another year, that they may adjust the number of months God hath forbidden, thus they allow what God hath forbidden; the evil of their deeds hath been made fairseeming to them; And verily God guideth not the infidel people.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَا لَكُمْ اِذَا قِيْلَ لَكُمُ انْفِرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اثَّاقَلْتُمْ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ ؕ اَرَضِيْتُمْ بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا مِنَ الْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ فَمَا مَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ‏(38)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MAA LAKUM EZAA QEELA LAKOMUL ANFEROOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE ASSAAQALTUM ELAL ARZE AARAZEETUM BE-HAYAATID DUNYAA MENAL AAKHERATE FAMAA MATAAU’U HAYAATID DUNYAA FIL AAKHERATE ILLAA QALEELUN.\nO’ ye who believe! What aileth you that when it is said unto you, “Go ye forth (to fight) in the way of God,” ye incline heavily to earth; What! contend ye (yourselves) with the life of this world instead of the hereafter? but the provision of the life of this world compared to the hereafter, is but little.\nاِلَّا تَنْفِرُوْا يُعَذِّبْكُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا   ۙ وَّيَسْتَبْدِلْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْ وَلَا تَضُرُّوْهُ شَيْئًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(39)\nILLAA TANFEROOA QABLO A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA WWAYASTABDEL QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM WA LAA TAZURROOHU SHAY-ANW WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nUnless ye go forth, He will chastise you with a painful chastisement and He will place in your place a people other than you, and no harm will ye do (unto) Him; and Verily God hath power over all things.\nاِلَّا تَنْصُرُوْهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللّٰهُ اِذْ اَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ثَانِىَ اثْنَيْنِ اِذْ هُمَا فِى الْغَارِ اِذْ يَقُوْلُ لِصَاحِبِهٖ لَا تَحْزَنْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَنَا ۚ فَاَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ سَكِيْنَتَهٗ عَلَيْهِ وَاَ يَّدَهٗ بِجُنُوْدٍ لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلٰى ؕ وَكَلِمَةُ اللّٰهِ هِىَ الْعُلْيَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(40)\nILLAA TANSUROOHU FAQAD NASARAHU LAAHO IZ AAKHRAJAHU LAZEENA KAFAROO SAANEAAA NAYNE IZ HUMAA FIL AL-GHAARE IZ YAQOOLO LESAAHEBEH LAA TAHZAN INNAL LAAHA MAA’ANAA FA ANZALAS LAAHO SAKEENATAHU A’LAYHE WA YYADAH BEJONOODIL LAM TARAWHAA WA KALEMATAT LAZEENA KAFARUL AS-SUFLAA WAKALEMATU LAAHE HEYA AL-U’ULYAA WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nIf ye help not him (the Prophet), (It matters not) for indeed God helped him when expelled him those who dis-believed, he was the second of the two, when they both were in the cave, when he said unto his Companion: “Fear thou not, verily God is with us,” So God sent down tranquillity upon him, and strengthened him with hosts (of angels) ye saw them not and made the word of those who believed not, the abased, and the word of God, that is the most Exalted; and verily, God is All-Mighty All-Wise.\nاِنْفِرُوْا خِفَافًا وَّثِقَالًا وَّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِكُمْ وَاَنْفُسِكُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(41)\nAENFEROOA KHEFAAFAN WWASEQAALAN WWAJAAHEDOOA BE-ANWAALEKUM WA ANFOSEKUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE ZAA ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nGo ye forth (with) light and heavy equipment and strive in the way of God with your property and your selves, this is better for you, if ye know (it).\nلَوْ كَانَ عَرَضًا قَرِيْبًا وَّسَفَرًا قَاصِدًا لَّاتَّبَعُوْكَ وَلٰكِنْۢ بَعُدَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الشُّقَّةُ  ؕ وَسَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَوِ اسْتَطَعْنَا لَخَرَجْنَا مَعَكُمْ ۚ يُهْلِكُوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(42)\nLAW KAANA A’ARAZAN QAREEBAA WWASAFARAN QAASEDAN LLAATTABAU’OOKA WA LAAKIL BAU’UDAT A’LAYHEMUL ASH-SHUQQATU WASAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAWE ASTATAA’NAA LAKHARAJNAA MA-A’KUM YUHLEKOONA ANFOSAHUM WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nHad there been immediate gain and the journey easy, certainly would they have followed thee, but the distance was too long for them; yet while they swear by God (saying) “Had we been able, we had surely gone with thee:” They cause their own selves to perish, and God knoweth that verily they are liars.\nعَفَا اللّٰهُ عَنْكَۚ لِمَ اَذِنْتَ لَهُمْ حَتّٰى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكَ الَّذِيْنَ صَدَقُوْا وَتَعْلَمَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(43)\nA’AFAA LAAHO A’NKAL LEMA AAZENTA LAHUM HATTAA YATABAYYANA LAKA LAZEENA SADAQOO WATAA’LAMA KAAZEBEEN.\nGod forgive thee (O’ Our Apostle!) Why didst thou give them leave (to stay behind) until it was manifest unto thee those who spake the truth, and thou hadst known the liars.\nلَا يَسْتَاْذِنُكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ اَنْ يُّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(44)\nLAA YASTAAZENUKA LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE AN YYUJAAHEDOOA BEAAMWAALEHEM WAANFUSEHEM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BE-MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nThey ask not leave of thee, who believe in God and the Last Day (of Judgment) (to be exempt) from striving with their wealth and their selves; Verily God is the knower of the pious ones.\nاِنَّمَا يَسْتَاْذِنُكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَارْتَابَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ فَهُمْ فِىْ رَيْبِهِمْ يَتَرَدَّدُوْنَ‏(45)\nINNAMAA YASTAAZENUKA LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WAARTAABAT QULOOBUHUM FAHUM FEE RAYBEHEM YATARADDADOONA.\nOnly they ask leave of thee (to be exempt) who believe not in God and the Last Day (of Judgment), and their hearts are in doubt, hence in their doubt they are tossed to and fro.\nوَلَوْ اَرَادُوْا الْخُرُوْجَ لَاَعَدُّوْا لَهٗ عُدَّةً وَّلٰكِنْ كَرِهَ اللّٰهُ انۢبِعَاثَهُمْ فَثَبَّطَهُمْ وَقِيْلَ اقْعُدُوْا مَعَ الْقٰعِدِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAW AARAADOOA AL-KHUROOJA LAAA’ADDOOA LAHU U’UDDATAN LAAKIL KAREHA LAAHO ANBEA’AASAHUM FASABBATAHUM WA QEELAD AQU’UDOOA LAAHA AL-QAAE’EDEENA.\nAnd had they (really) intended to go forth, they would certainly have made preparations for it, but God was averse to their going forth, so He withheld them and it was said (unto them) “Sit ye (still) with those who sit (idle).\nلَوْ خَرَجُوْا فِيْكُمْ مَّا زَادُوْكُمْ اِلَّا خَبَالًا وَّلَاْاَوْضَعُوْا خِلٰلَكُمْ يَبْغُوْنَكُمُ الْفِتْنَةَ ۚ وَفِيْكُمْ سَمّٰعُوْنَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(47)\nLAW KHARAJOO FEEKUM MAA ZAADOOKUM ILLAA KHABAALAN WWALAAAAWZAU’OOA KHELAALAKUM YABGHOONAKUMU FITNATA WA FEEKUM SAMMAAU’OONA LAHUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nHad they gone forth with you they would not have added to you aught save mischief, and they would have certainly hurried about (to and fro) amidst you, to sow dissensions amidst you and among you there are those who hearken for their sake; And God knoweth the unjust.\nلَقَدِ ابْتَغَوُا الْفِتْنَةَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَقَلَّبُوْا لَكَ الْاُمُوْرَ حَتّٰى جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَظَهَرَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ وَهُمْ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(48)\nLAQADE ABTAGHAWUA FITNATA MIN QABLO WAQALLABOOA LAKA AL-AUMOORA HATTAA JAAA-A HAQQO WA ZAHARAL AMRUL LAAHE WA HUM KAAREHOONA.\nCertainly, did they seek (to sow) dissension before they upset matters for thee, until came the truth and did prevail the decree of God, though they were averse (from it).\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ ائْذَنْ لِّىْ وَلَا تَفْتِنِّىْ ؕ اَلَا فِى الْفِتْنَةِ سَقَطُوْا ؕ وَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمُحِيْطَةٌ ۢ بِالْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(49)\nWA MINHUM MAN YAQOOLO AZAN LEE WA LAA TAFTENNEAA ALAA FIL AL-FETNATE SAQATOOA WA INNA JAHANNAMA LA-MOHEETATUM BIL-KAAFEREEN.\nAmong them there is (many) a man who says, exempt me, and try me not; Surely into trial have they already fallen; and verily hell encompasseth the infidels.\nاِنْ تُصِبْكَ حَسَنَةٌ تَسُؤْهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْكَ مُصِيْبَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا قَدْ اَخَذْنَاۤ اَمْرَنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَيَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ فَرِحُوْنَ‏(50)\nIN TUSEBKA HASANATUL TASUHUM WA TUSEBKA MUSEEBATUN YAQOOLOO QAD AKHAZNAA AAMRANAA MIN QABLO WAYATAWALLAWA WA HUM FAREEHOON.\nIf befalleth thee (any) good, it grieveth them, and if afflicteth thee (any) hardship, say they “indeed we had taken care of our affair before,” and turn they away and they rejoice.\nقُلْ لَّنْ يُّصِيْبَنَاۤ اِلَّا مَا كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَنَا ۚ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮنَا  ۚ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(51)\nQUL LAN-Y YYUSEEBANAA ILLAA MAA KATABAL LAAHO LANAA HOWA MAWLAANAA WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nSay: (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Never shall afflict us (anything) save what God hath decreed for us; He is our (Liege) Lord; and on God should the believers rely.\nقُلْ هَلْ تَرَبَّصُوْنَ بِنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِحْدَى الْحُسْنَيَيْنِؕ وَنَحْنُ نَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمْ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِعَذَابٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖۤ اَوْ بِاَيْدِيْنَا  ۖ  فَتَرَبَّصُوْۤا اِنَّا مَعَكُمْ مُّتَرَبِّصُوْنَ‏(52)\nQUL HAL TARABBASOONA LAKHASAFA ILLAA EHDAB AL-HUSNAYAYNE WA NAHNO NATARABBASU BEKUM AN YYUSEEBAKUMU LAAHO BE-A’ZAABIN MIN I’NDEHI AW BE-AYDEENAA FATARABBASOOA INNAA MA-A’KUM MMUTARABBESOONA.\nSay: “What! await ye for us aught but one of the two excellent things (either victory or Martyrdom)? and we await for you that God afflicteth you with chastisement from Himself or from our hands; Then wait ye, Verily we too with you will wait.\nقُلْ اَنْفِقُوْا طَوْعًا اَوْ كَرْهًا لَّنْ يُّتَقَبَّلَ مِنْكُمْؕ اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(53)\nQUL ANFEQOO TEYAA AW AW LAN-Y YYUTAQABBALA MENKUM INNAKUM KUNTUM QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nSay: “Spend ye willingly or reluctantly never shall it be accepted from you; (for) verily ye are (a) transgressing people.\nوَمَا مَنَعَهُمْ اَنْ تُقْبَلَ مِنْهُمْ نَفَقٰتُهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَبِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَلَا يَاْتُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ اِلَّا وَهُمْ كُسَالٰى وَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ اِلَّا وَهُمْ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA MAA MANAA’AHUM AN TUQBALA MINHUM NAFAQAATUHUM ILLAA ANNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WABERASOOLEH WA LAA YAATOONAL SALAATA ILLAA WA HUM KUSAALAA WA LAA YUNFEQOONA ILLAA WA HUM KAAREHOONA.\nAnd nothing hindereth the acceptance from them of their offerings save that they reject God and His Apostle (Muhammad) and they come not to prayer but sluggishly and spend not (in goodness) but reluctantly.\nفَلَا تُعْجِبْكَ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْؕ اِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ بِهَا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَتَزْهَقَ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(55)\nFALAA TUA’JEBKA AAMWAALUHUM WA LAA AAWLAADUHUM INNAMAA YOREEDO LAAHO LEEA’AZZEBAHUM BEHAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WATAZHAQA ANFOSOHUM WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nLet not therefore amaze thee, their wealth nor their issues; Indeed, intendeth God (only) to torment them with these (things) in the life of (this) world and that their souls depart while they are disbelievers.\nوَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ اِنَّهُمْ لَمِنْكُمْؕ وَمَا هُمْ مِّنْكُمْ وَلٰكِنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ يَّفْرَقُوْنَ‏(56)\nWAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE INNAHUM LAMENKUM WA MAA HUM MINKUM WALAAKENNAHUM QAWMUN YYAFRAQOONA.\nAnd they swear by God that they are surely of you; While they are not of you but they are people afraid (of you).\nلَوْ يَجِدُوْنَ مَلْجَاً اَوْ مَغٰرٰتٍ اَوْ مُدَّخَلًا لَّوَلَّوْا اِلَيْهِ وَهُمْ يَجْمَحُوْنَ‏(57)\nLAW YAJEDOONA MALJAA AW MAGHAARAATIN AW MUDDAKHALAN LLAWALLAWA ELAYHE WA HUM YAJMAHOONA.\nIf they could find a refuge, or caves or a place to enter (conceal themselves) therein, certainly would they have turned themselves unto it, rushing thereto (in haste).\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّلْمِزُكَ فِى الصَّدَقٰتِ ۚ فَاِنْ اُعْطُوْا مِنْهَا رَضُوْا وَاِنْ لَّمْ يُعْطَوْا مِنْهَاۤ اِذَا هُمْ يَسْخَطُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYALMEZUKA FIL SADAQAATE FA-IN AUA’TOOA MINHAA RAZOOA WA LAM YUA’TAWA MINHAA EZAA HUM YASKHATOONA.\nAnd of them are those who blame thee with regard to the (distribution of) alms; if they are given from it they are pleased, and if not given to them from it, Behold! they are enraged.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ رَضُوْا مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗۙ وَقَالُوْا حَسْبُنَا اللّٰهُ سَيُؤْتِيْنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَ رَسُوْلُهٗۙ اِنَّاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رٰغِبُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM RAZOOA MAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU WA QAALOO HASBUNAA LAAHO SAYUTEENAA LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WA RASOOLUH INNAA ELAL LAAHE RAAGHEBOONA.\nAnd if only they were content with what God and His Apostle had given them and had said: “Sufficient for us is God! Soon will give us God of His grace and His Apostle too; verily unto God (alone) do we (all) turn (in our hopes)\nاِنَّمَا الصَّدَقٰتُ لِلْفُقَرَآءِ وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَالْعٰمِلِيْنَ عَلَيْهَا وَالْمُؤَلَّفَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَفِى الرِّقَابِ وَالْغٰرِمِيْنَ وَفِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِؕ فَرِيْضَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(60)\nINNAMAA AS-SADAQAATU LIL-FOQARAAA-IL WAL MASAAKEENE WA A’AMELEENAL A’LAYHAA WAL MUALLAFATE QULOOBUHUM WA FIR REQAAB WAL GHAAREMEENA WA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAB NIS SABEEL FAREEZATANW MENAL LAAH WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nVerily alms are only for the poor and the needy and the workers (in the administration of the poor-rate) and those whose heart’s alliance is sought and (the ransoming of) the captives, and those in debt, and in the way of God and the way-farer; a duty ordained by God; And God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَمِنْهُمُ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ النَّبِىَّ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هُوَ اُذُنٌ ؕ قُلْ اُذُنُ خَيْرٍ لَّكُمْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَيُؤْمِنُ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَرَحْمَةٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(61)\nWAMENHUMU LAZEENA YOAZOONAL NABIYYA WA YAQOOLOONA HOWA AUZUNUN QUL AUZUNU KHAYRIN LAKUM BIL LAAHE BIL-LAAHE WA BIL LAAHE LIL-MOAMENEEN WA RAHMAH LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM WAL LAZEENA YOAZOONAL TOAZOO LAAHE LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nAmong them are those who hurt the Apostle (Muhammad) and say they (that) “he is (all)-ear” (i.e., one who believes in everything he hears); say (he Muhammad,) is the Ear of good for you; he believeth in God and hath faith in the believers and a mercy unto those of you who believe, and those who hurt the Apostle of God (Muhammad) for them is a grievous chastisement.\nيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَكُمْ لِيُرْضُوْكُمْۚ وَاللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗۤ اَحَقُّ اَنْ يُّرْضُوْهُ اِنْ كَانُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(62)\nYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAKUM LEERZOOKUM WAL LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU AHAQQO AN YYURZOOHU IN KAANOO MUMENEENA.\nSwear they by God unto you that they might please you; and (whereas) God and His Apostle (Muhammad) hath a greater right that they should please Him, if they are believers.\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّهٗ مَنْ يُّحَادِدِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاَنَّ لَهٗ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خَالِدًا فِيْهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْخِزْىُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(63)\nALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAHU MAN YYUHAADEDE LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA ANNAL LAHU NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDAN FEEHAA ZAA LEKA AL-KHEZAAU A’ZEEM.\nKnow they not that whoso opposeth God and His Apostle (Muhammad) verily for him is the fire of Hell to abide therein? that is the grievous abasement.\nيَحْذَرُ الْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ اَنْ تُنَزَّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُوْرَةٌ تُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ ؕ قُلِ اسْتَهْزِءُوْا ۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مُخْرِجٌ مَّا تَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(64)\nYAHZARU MONAAFEQOONA AN TUNAZZALA A’LAYHIM SOORATUN TUNABBEUHUM BEMAA FEE QOLOOBEHIM QOLIL ASTAHZEOOA INNAL LAAHA MUKHREJUM MAA TAHZAROONA.\nThe hypocrites fear lest a ‘Sura ’ should be sent about them declaring openly unto them what is (there really) in their hearts; Say! “Scoff ye! verily God bringeth forth what ye fear.\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوْضُ وَنَلْعَبُؕ قُلْ اَبِاللّٰهِ وَاٰيٰتِهٖ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(65)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM LAYAQOOLUNNAL INNAMAA KUNNAA NAKHOOZU WANALA’ABU QUL AABEALLLAAHE WA AAYAATEHI WA RASOOLEHI KUNTUM TASTAHZEOONA.\nIf ye question them, surely will say they “We were only discoursing and jesting;” Say! What at God, His signs and His Apostles, scoff ye?\nلَا تَعْتَذِرُوْا قَدْ كَفَرْتُمْ بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِكُمْ ؕ اِنْ نَّعْفُ عَنْ طَآئِفَةٍ مِّنْكُمْ نُعَذِّبْ طَآئِفَةً ۢ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(66)\nLAA TAA’TAZEROOA QAD KAFARTUM BA’DA EEMAANEKUM IN NNAA’FU A’N TAAEFATIN MINKUM NUA’AZZEB YASTAZ-E’FO BE-ANNAHUM KAANOO MUJREMEEN.\nMake ye not excuses, indeed ye have denied after ye had believed; If We pardon a party of you, we will chastise (another) party (of you) for surely, they are the guilty ones.\nاَلْمُنٰفِقُوْنَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْضٍۘ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمُنْكَرِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَقْبِضُوْنَ اَيْدِيَهُمْؕ نَسُوا اللّٰهَ فَنَسِيَهُمْؕ اِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(67)\nAALMUNAAFEQOONA WAL MUNAAFEQAATU KHALAA MIN ELAA YAAMUROONA BIL-MUNKARE WAYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MAA’ROOFE WAYAQBEZOONA AAYDEEHUM NASUL LAAHA FANASEEHUM INNAL MONAAFEQEENA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nThe hypocrite men and the hypocrite women are one from another, they enjoin evil and forbid good and withhold their hands (from spending in the way of God); They have forsaken God, so He hath forsaken them; verily the hypocrites, they are the transgressors.\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتِ وَالْكُفَّارَ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ هِىَ حَسْبُهُمْ ۚ وَلَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ ۙ‏(68)\nWA-A’DAR LAAHO MONAAFEQEENA WAL-MONAAFEQAATE WA KUFFAARA NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA HEYA HASBUHUM WA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\nGod hath promised the hypocrite men and the hypocrite women and the disbelievers the fire of Hell to abide therein; this sufficieth for them; and God hath cursed them, and for them is the chastisement (which shall be) lasting.\nكَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ كَانُوْۤا اَشَدَّ مِنْكُمْ قُوَّةً وَّاَكْثَرَ اَمْوَالًا وَّاَوْلَادًا ؕ فَاسْتَمْتَعُوْا بِخَلَاقِهِمْ فَاسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِخَلَاقِكُمْ كَمَا اسْتَمْتَعَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ بِخَلَاقِهِمْ وَخُضْتُمْ كَالَّذِىْ خَاضُوْا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(69)\nTAKOONOO MIN QABLEKUM KAANOO ASHADDA MINKUM QUWWAH WWAAKSARA AAMWAALAN WWAAWLAADAN FAASTAMTAU’OOA BEKHALAAQEHEM FAASTAMTAA’TUM BEKHALAAQEKUM KAMAA ASTAMTAA’A LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM BEKHALAAQEHEM WAKHUZTUM KALLAZEE KHAAZOOA AOOLAAEKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\n(O’ Hypocrites! ye are) Like those (who flourished) before you; they were stronger than you in strength and more abundant in wealth and children; so they enjoyed their portion; thus have ye enjoyed your portion as those before you did enjoy their portion, and ye indulge in vain discourses as those (before you) (in vain) did indulge in; These are those whose works have come to naught in this world and the hereafter; and these are they the losers.\nاَلَمْ يَاْتِهِمْ نَبَاُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ  ۙ وَقَوْمِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاَصْحٰبِ مَدْيَنَ وَالْمُؤْتَفِكٰتِ ؕ اَتَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ۚ فَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(70)\nALAM YAATEHEM NABAA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM QAWME NOOHIN WWAA’AADIN WA WA QAWME IBRAAHEEMA WA ASHAABIL MADYANA WAL MUTAFEKAATE AATATHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA KAANA LAAHO LE-YAZLEMAHUM WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nWhat! came not unto them the news of those before them; of the people of Noah and ‘Ad and Thamud’, the people of Abraham and the inhabitants of Midian and the cities over-thrown; came unto them their apostles with clear proofs (of their truthfulness) Thus it was not God to do injustice unto them, but they unto themselves were unjust.\nوَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتُ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍۘ يَاْمُرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَيُطِيْعُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ سَيَرْحَمُهُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(71)\nWAL MO’MENOONA WAL MUMENAATU KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O ELAA YAAMUROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WAYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WAYUTEEU’OONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAH AOOLAAEKA SAYARHAMUHUMU LAAH INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAnd the believer men and the believer women, they arc guardians to one another; they enjoin good and forbid evil and they establish (the regular) prayer and pay the poor-rate and obey God and His Apostle (Muhammad), These, God will bestow on them His mercy; Verily God is All-Mighty, All-Wise.\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا وَمَسٰكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِىْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ ؕ وَرِضْوَانٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(72)\nWA-A’DAR LAAHO MOAMENEEN WAL-MOAMENAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAMASAAKENA TAYBATAN FEE JANNATIN A’ADNIN WAREZWAANUN MENAL LAAHE AKBARO ZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nGod hath promised to the believer men and the believer women gardens ‘neath which flow the rivers, to abide in them, and the excellent mansions in the gardens of ‘Adn ’ But the good-will of God is the greatest; That is the grand achievement.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ جَاهِدِ الْكُفَّارَ وَالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَاغْلُظْ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(73)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO JAAHEDE KUFFAARA KAAFEREENA WAAGHLUZ WA WA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MASEER.\nO’ (Our) Apostle (Muhammad)! strive hard against the infidels and the hypocrites, and be severe unto them; and their abode shall be hell; and (what) an evil destination it is.\nيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ مَا قَالُوْا ؕ وَلَقَدْ قَالُوْا كَلِمَةَ الْكُفْرِ وَكَفَرُوْا بَعْدَ اِسْلَامِهِمْ وَهَمُّوْا بِمَا لَمْ يَنَالُوْا ۚ وَمَا نَقَمُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اَغْنٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ۚ فَاِنْ يَّتُوْبُوْا يَكُ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ يَّتَوَلَّوْا يُعَذِّبْهُمُ اللّٰهُ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا ۙ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَمَا لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(74)\nYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE MAA QAALOO WA LAQAD QAALOO KALEMATAT AL-KUFRE WA KAFAROO BA’DA AESLAAMEHEM WAHAMMOOA BEMAA LAM YANAALOO WA MAA NAQAMOO ILLAA AN AAGHNAAHUMU LAAHO WA RASOOLOHU MIN FAZLEHI FA-IN YYATOOBOOA YAKU KHAYRAN LAHUM WA YYATAWALLAWA YUA’AZZEBHUMU LAAHO A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WA MAA LAHUM FIL ARZE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nSwear they by God that they uttered not (what they are charged with) (although) they did utter the word of infidelity, and disbelieved after their (embracing) Islam, and they designed what they could not achieve, and they did not seek revenge but because God and His Apostle had enriched them by His grace; If they repent it will be good for them, and if they turn back God will chastise them with a painful chastisement in this world and the hereafter; and there shall not be for them on earth any protector or a helper.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ عَاهَدَ اللّٰهَ لَئِنْ اٰتٰٮنَا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ لَنَصَّدَّقَنَّ وَلَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA MINHUM MAN A’AAHADA LAAHA LAIL AAATAANAA MIN FAZLEHI LANASSADDAQANNA WALANAKOONANNA MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd of them are those who made a covenant with God; “If He giveth us out of His grace, we will certainly give alms and we will certainly be of the righteous ones.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ بَخِلُوْا بِهٖ وَتَوَلَّوْا وَّهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA AAATAAHUM MIN FAZLEHI BAKHELOOA BEHI WA TAWALLAW WA HUM MO’REZOON.\nBut when He did give them out of His grace, they became niggardly with it and they turned back, averse.\nفَاَعْقَبَهُمْ نِفَاقًا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يَلْقَوْنَهٗ بِمَاۤ اَخْلَفُوا اللّٰهَ مَا وَعَدُوْهُ وَبِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْذِبُوْنَ‏(77)\nFAAA’QABAHUM NEFAAQAN FEE QOLOOBEHIM ELAA YAWMIL YALQAWNAHU BEMAA AAKHLAFOOA LAAHA MAA WAA’ADOOHU WA BEMAA KAANOO YAKZEBOON.\nSo in consequence hath He effected hypocrisy in their hearts till the day when they shall meet Him because they had failed to fulfil unto God what they had promised unto Him and because of what they used to lie (continuously).\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ سِرَّهُمْ وَنَجْوٰٮهُمْ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ ۚ‏(78)\nALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO SERRAHUM WANAJWAAHUM WA ANNAL LAAHA A’ALLAAMU AL-GHUYOOBE.\nWhat! know not they that God knoweth their hidden thoughts and their secret whisperings, and that God is the Greatest Knower of (everything) unseen.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَلْمِزُوْنَ الْمُطَّوِّعِيْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ فِى الصَّدَقٰتِ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ اِلَّا جُهْدَهُمْ فَيَسْخَرُوْنَ مِنْهُمْؕ سَخِرَ اللّٰهُ مِنْهُمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(79)\nLAZEENA YALMEZOONA AL-MUTTAWE’EENA MENAL MOAMENEEN FIL SADAQAATE WAL LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA ILLAA JUHDAHUM FAYASKHAROONA MENHUM SAKHERA LAAHO MINHUM WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThose who traduce the free givers of charity among the believers and them who find not anything (to give) but their hard earnings, so they scoff at them; God will scoff’ at them and for them shall be a painful chastisement.\nاِسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ اَوْ لَا تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْؕ اِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِيْنَ مَرَّةً فَلَنْ يَّغْفِرَ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْؕ ذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(80)\nAESTAGHFER LAHUM AW LAA TASTAGHFIR LAHUM IN TASTAGHFIR LAHUM SABE’EENA MARRATAN FALAN YAGHFERAL LAAHO LAHUM ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WARASOOLEH WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ FAASEQEEN.\nSeek thou (O’ Our Apostle!) forgiveness for them or seekest thou not forgiveness for them, (the same will it be); if thou seeketh forgiveness for them seventy times, never will God forgive them; This because they disbelieved in God and in His Apostle (Muhammad!) and God guideth not the transgressing people.\nفَرِحَ الْمُخَلَّفُوْنَ بِمَقْعَدِهِمْ خِلٰفَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَكَرِهُوْۤا اَنْ يُّجَاهِدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَقَالُوْا لَا تَنْفِرُوْا فِى الْحَرِّؕ قُلْ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ اَشَدُّ حَرًّاؕ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(81)\nFAREHA MOKHALLAFOONA BEMAQA’ADEHEM KHELAAFA RASOOLIL LAAHE WAKAREHOOA AN YYUJAAHEDOOA BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA QAALOO LAA TANFEROOA FIL AL-HARR QUL NAARUL JAHANNAMA ASHADDO HARRAN LAW KAANOO YAFQAHOON.\nDelighted were the ones left behind (in the expedition of ‘Tabuk’) for their sitting (in-active) behind God’s apostle and they were averse from striving in God’s way with their wealth and their selves, and said they (to the others) “Go ye not in the heat;” Say thou! “The fire of Hell is fiercer in heat;” If only they could understand.\nفَلْيَضْحَكُوْا قَلِيْلاً وَّلْيَبْكُوْا كَثِيْرًا ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(82)\nFALYAZHAKOOA QALEELAAN WWALYABKOOA KASEERAA JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nTherefore, they shall laugh little and weep much (as) a recompense for what they used to earn.\nفَاِنْ رَّجَعَكَ اللّٰهُ اِلٰى طَآئِفَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ فَاسْتَاْذَنُوْكَ لِلْخُرُوْجِ فَقُلْ لَّنْ تَخْرُجُوْا مَعِىَ اَبَدًا وَّلَنْ تُقَاتِلُوْا مَعِىَ عَدُوًّا ؕ اِنَّكُمْ رَضِيْتُمْ بِالْقُعُوْدِ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ فَاقْعُدُوْا مَعَ الْخٰلِفِيْنَ‏(83)\nFA-IN RRAJAA’AKA LAAHO ELAA TAAEFATIN MINHUM FAASTAAZANOOKA LIL-KHUROOJE FAQUL LAN-Y TAKHRUJOOA MA-E’YA ABADAM WWALAN TOQAATELOO MA-E’YA A’DUWWAL INNAKUM RAZEETUM BIL-QUU’OODE AWWALA MARRAH FAAQU’UDOOA LAAHA AL-KHAALEFEENA.\nIf God bringeth thee back to a party of them, then they seek thy permission to go forth, say thou “ye shall never go forth with me and ye shall never fight an enemy with me; verily ye chose to sit (idle) the first time, then sit (now also idle) with those who stay behind.\nوَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلٰٓى اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ مَّاتَ اَبَدًا وَّلَا تَقُمْ عَلٰى قَبْرِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ فٰسِقُوْنَ‏(84)\nWA LAA TUSALLE A’LAA AHADIM MINHUM MMAATA ABADAM WA LAA TAQUM A’LAA QABREH INNAHUM KAFAROO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA MAATOO WA HUM FAASEQOONA.\nAnd pray thou not at all on any one of them who dieth and nor stand thee ever at his grave; (for) verily they disbelieved in God and His Apostle and died they as wicked ones.\nوَلَا تُعْجِبْكَ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَاَوْلَادُهُمْؕ اِنَّمَا يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّعَذِّبَهُمْ بِهَا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَتَزْهَقَ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA LAA TUA’JEBKA AAMWAALUHUM WAAWLAADUHUM INNAMAA YOREEDO LAAHO AN YYUA’AZZEBAHUM BEHAA FIL DUNYAA WATAZHAQA ANFOSOHUM WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nLet not their wealth and their children astonish thee; Verily God only wisheth to chastise them with these in this world and that their soul should depart while they are infidels.\nوَاِذَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ اَنْ اٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَجَاهِدُوْا مَعَ رَسُوْلِهِ اسْتَاْذَنَكَ اُولُوا الطَّوْلِ مِنْهُمْ وَقَالُوْا ذَرْنَا نَكُنْ مَّعَ الْقٰعِدِيْنَ‏(86)\nWA EZAA UNZELAT SOORATUN AN AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WAJAAHEDOOA LAAHA RASOOLEHE ASTAAZANAKA ULUL AT-TAWLE MINHUM WA QAALOO ZARNAA NAKUN MA-A’L AL-QAAE’EDEENA.\nAnd whenever a ‘sura’ is revealed (enjoining) that (they should) believe in God and strive hard along with His Apostle; those with abundant means seek thy permission and say, “Leave us (behind) we may be with those who sit (at home).\nرَضُوْا بِاَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الْخَوَالِفِ وَطُبِعَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(87)\nRAZOOA BOYOOTA YYAKOONOOA LAAHA AL-KHAWAALEFE WATUBEA’A A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YAFQAHOON.\nPrefer they to be with those (women children and the sick) who stay behind for a seal hath been set on their hearts there-fore they understand not.\nلٰكِنِ الرَّسُوْلُ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ جَاهَدُوْا بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْؕ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ الْخَيْرٰتُ وَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(88)\nLAAKENE RASOOLO WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU JAAHADOO BEAAMWAALEHEM WAANFUSEHEM WAAWLAAEKA LAHOMUL AL-KHAYRAATU WAAWLAAEKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nBut the Apostle and those who believe with him strive hard (fight) with their wealth and their selves; And these, for them are (all) good things; And these, they are the successful ones.\nاَعَدَّ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(89)\nA-A’DDA LAAHO LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nGod hath prepared for them gardens ‘neath which flow rivers to abide therein; that is the great achievement.\nوَ جَآءَ الْمُعَذِّرُوْنَ مِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ لِيُؤْذَنَ لَهُمْ وَقَعَدَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ؕ سَيُصِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(90)\nWA JAAA-A AL-MUA’AZZEROONA MENAL A-A’RAABE LEEZANA LAHUM WAQAA’ADA LAZEENA KAZABOOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU SAYUSEEBU LAZEENA KAFAROO MINHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nAnd came with excuses from the dwellers of the desert that permission may be given to them, and sat (at home) those who lied to God and His Apostle; unto those of them who disbelieved shall shortly reach a grievous chastisement.\nلَيْسَ عَلَى الضُّعَفَآءِ وَلَا عَلَى الْمَرْضٰى وَلَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ حَرَجٌ اِذَا نَصَحُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَ رَسُوْلِهٖؕ مَا عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ مِنْ سَبِيْلٍؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ‏(91)\nLAYSA A’LAL AZ-ZUA’AFAAE WA LAA A’LAL AL-MARZAA WA LAA A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA MAA YUNFEQOONA HARAJUN EZAA NASAHOOA LILLAAHE WA RASOOLEH MAA A’LAL MOHSENEEN MIN SABEELIN WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\n(It) shall not be on the weak nor on the sick nor on those who find not what they should spend, a task when they are sincere to God and His Apostle; And against the doers of good there is no way (to claim); and God is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.\nوَّلَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا مَاۤ اَتَوْكَ لِتَحْمِلَهُمْ قُلْتَ لَاۤ اَجِدُ مَاۤ اَحْمِلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ تَوَلَّوْا وَّاَعْيُنُهُمْ تَفِيْضُ مِنَ الدَّمْعِ حَزَنًا اَلَّا يَجِدُوْا مَا يُنْفِقُوْنَؕ‏(92)\nWA LAA A’LAL LAZEENA EZAA MAA AATAWKA LETAHMELAHUM QULTA LAA AAJEDU MAA AAHMELUKUM A’LAYHE TAWALLAW WWAAA’YUNUHUM TAFEEZU MENAL AD-DAME’E HAZANAN ALLAA YAJEDOOA MAA ZAA YUNFEQOON.\nNor (is the task) on those unto whom when they came unto thee to provide them with mounts, thou didst say, “I find not means to carry you;” They went hack with their eyes overflowed with tears sorrowful that they find not means to spend (in the cause).\nاِنَّمَا السَّبِيْلُ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَاْذِنُوْنَكَ وَهُمْ اَغْنِيَآءُۚ رَضُوْا بِاَنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الْخَوَالِفِۙ وَطَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(93)\nINNAMAA AS-SABEELU A’LAL LAZEENA YASTAAZENOONAKA WA HUM AAGHNEEAAAU RAZOOA BOYOOTA YYAKOONOOA LAAHA AL-KHAWAALEFE WATABAA’A LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nVerily the way (to charge) is only against those who seek thy permission (to stay behind) while they are rich; prefer they to be with those who remain behind (Women, Children and the sick) and (it is as if) God hath set seal upon their hearts, thus they know not (what they miss).\nيَعْتَذِرُوْنَ اِلَيْكُمْ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ ؕ قُلْ لَّا تَعْتَذِرُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكُمْ قَدْ نَبَّاَنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْ اَخْبَارِكُمْ ؕ وَ سَيَرَى اللّٰهُ عَمَلَكُمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ ثُمَّ تُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(94)\nYAA’TAZEROONA ELAYKUM EZAA RAJAA’TUM ELAYHIM QUL LAA TAA’TAZEROOA LAN NOAMENA LAKUM QAD NABBAANAA LAAHO MIN AAKHBAAREKUM WA SA-YARAL LAAHO A’AMALAKUM WA RASOOLOHU SUMMA TORADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThey will make excuses unto you when ye return unto them (after the expedition)’, Say thou (O’ Our Apostle) “Make ye no excuses (now), by no means will we believe you, Indeed God hath informed us of the matter of (the truth) about you; And now God will behold your doings and (also) His Apostle, then shall ye be returned unto the Knower of (everything) hidden and the manifest, then ye will be informed of (all) what ye were doing.\nسَيَحْلِفُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اِذَا انْقَلَبْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ لِتُعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمْؕ فَاَعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمْؕ اِنَّهُمْ رِجْسٌ وَّمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(95)\nSAYAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE LAKUM EZAA ANQALABTUM ELAYHIM LETUA’REZOOA A’ANHUM FAAA’REZOOA A’ANHUM INNAHUM REJSUN WWAMAAWAAHUM JAHANNAMUL JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nThey will swear unto you by God, when ye return unto them, that ye may turn aside from them; so turn ye aside from them; verily they are unclean and their abode is hell; a recompense for what they did earn.\nيَحْلِفُوْنَ لَكُمْ لِتَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْۚ فَاِنْ تَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَرْضٰى عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(96)\nYAHLEFOONA LAKUM LETARZAWA A’NHUM FA-IN TARZAWA A’NHUM FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YARZAA A’NIL QAWMIL FAASEQEEN.\nThey will swear unto you that ye may be pleased with them, but (even) if ye be pleased with them, verily God is not pleased with people (who are) wicked.\nاَلْاَعْرَابُ اَشَدُّ كُفْرًا وَّ نِفَاقًا وَّاَجْدَرُ اَلَّا يَعْلَمُوْا حُدُوْدَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(97)\nAALAAA’RAABU ASHADDO KUFRAN WA NEFAAQAN WWAAJDARU ALLAA YAA’LAMOOA HODOODAL MAA ANZALAL LAAHO A’LAA RASOOLEH WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nThe (rustic) Arabs (of the desert) are very hard in infidelity and hypocrisy, and more inclined not to know the limits what God hath sent down unto His Apostle; And God is All Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَمِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مَنْ يَّتَّخِذُ مَا يُنْفِقُ مَغْرَمًا وَّيَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمُ الدَّوَآئِرَؕ عَلَيْهِمْ دَآئِرَةُ السَّوْءِؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(98)\nWA MENAN A-A’RAABE MAN YATTAKHEZO MAA YUNFEQO MAGHRAMAN WWAYATARABBASU BEKOMUL AD-DAWAAERA A’LAYHIM DAA-ERATUS SAW WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd of the (rustic) Arabs (of the desert ) are those who take what they spend to be a fine, and they wait for calamities (to befall) unto you; On them (shall be) the evil calamity; And God is All Hearing, All-Knowing.\nوَمِنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَيَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنْفِقُ قُرُبٰتٍ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَصَلَوٰتِ الرَّسُوْلِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهَا قُرْبَةٌ لَّهُمْؕ سَيُدْخِلُهُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(99)\nWA MENAN A-A’RAABE MAN YOAMENO BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WAYATTAKHEZU MAA YUNFEQO QURUBAATIN I’NDAL LAAHE WASALAWTE AR-RASOOLE ALAA INNAHAA QURBATUN LAHUM SAYUDKHELUHUMU LAAHO FEE FEE INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd of the (rustic) Arabs (of the desert) are those who believe in God and the Last Day (of Judgment) and deem what they spend to be (the means of) approach unto God and the prayers (blessings) of the Apostle; Verily it shall be the means of approach for them; soon shall God admit them into His mercy; Verily God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nوَالسّٰبِقُوْنَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ وَالْاَنْصَارِ وَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُمْ بِاِحْسَانٍ ۙ رَّضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ وَاَعَدَّ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ تَحْتَهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(100)\nWAS-SAABEQOONAS AWWALOON MENAL MOHAAJEREENAL WAL AANSAARE WAL LAZEENA ATTABAU’OOHUM BE-EHSAAN RRAZEAAA LAAHO A’NHUM WARAZOOA A’NHO WA A-A’DDA LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE TAHTAHAA ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM ZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nAnd (as for) the foremost, the first of the ‘Muhajirs ‘ and the ‘Ansars ‘, and those who followed them in goodness, God is well-pleased with them and they are well-pleased with Him, and He hath prepared for them gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, to abide therein for ever; That is great achievement.\nوَمِمَّنْ حَوْلَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَعْرَابِ مُنٰفِقُوْنَ ۛؕ وَمِنْ اَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَةِ  ؔۛمَرَدُوْا عَلَى النِّفَاقِلَا تَعْلَمُهُمْ ؕ نَحْنُ نَعْلَمُهُمْ ؕ سَنُعَذِّبُهُمْ مَّرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عَذَابٍ عَظِيْمٍ ۚ‏(101)\nWA MIMMAN HAWLAKUM MENAL A-A’RAABE MUNAAFEQOONA WA MIN AHLIL MADEENATE MARADOOA A’LAL AN-NEFAAQELAA TAA’LAMUHUM NAHNO NAA’LAMUHUM SANUA’AZZEBUHUM MARRATAYNE SUMMA YORADDOONA ELAA A’ZAABIN A’ZEEM.\nAnd of those who are around you of the (rustic) Arabs (of the desert) there are hypocrites; and from the inhabitants of Madina (also); Stubborn are they in hypocrisy; Thou knowest them not, We know them; twice will We chastise them, then shall they be turned unto a grievous chastisement.\nوَاٰخَرُوْنَ اعْتَرَفُوْا بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ خَلَطُوْا عَمَلًا صَالِحًا وَّاٰخَرَ سَيِّئًا ؕ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّتُوْبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(102)\nWA AAKHAROONA AA’TARAFOOA BEZUNOOBEHEM KHALATOOA A’AMALAN SAALEHAN WWAAKHARA SAYAN A’ASAA LAAHO AN YYATOOBA A’LAYHIM INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd others have confessed their faults, they have mixed a good act with another (which is) evil; may be God will turn unto them (in mercy); Verily God is Oft-Forgiving, All- Merciful.\nخُذْ مِنْ اَمْوَالِهِمْ صَدَقَةً تُطَهِّرُهُمْ وَتُزَكِّيْهِمْ بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْؕ اِنَّ صَلٰوتَكَ سَكَنٌ لَّهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(103)\nKHUZ MIN AAMWAALEHEM SADAQATAN TUTAHHERUHUM WATUZAKKEEHEM BEHAA WASALLE WA INNAL SALAAWTAKA SAKANUN LAHUM WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nTake thou alms out of their wealth, thou wouldst cleanse them and purify them thereby, and pray for them; verily thy prayer is assurance (of peace) for them; And God is All-Hearing and All-Knowing.\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ يَقْبَلُ التَّوْبَةَ عَنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَاْخُذُ الصَّدَقٰتِ وَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(104)\nALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA YAQBALU AT-TAWBATA A’N E’BAADEHI WAYAAKHUZU SADAQAATE WA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nKnow they not that God is He who accepteth repentance from his bondmen and receiveth the alms, and God is verily He, The Oft-Returning (to mercy), The Most Merciful.\nوَقُلِ اعْمَلُوْا فَسَيَرَى اللّٰهُ عَمَلَكُمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَؕ وَسَتُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰى عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۚ‏(105)\nWA AA’MALOOA FASAYARAA LAAHO A’AMALAKUM WA RASOOLOHU WA KULLUN WASATURADDOONA ELAA A’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd say thou (unto them), Act ye as ye will, God beholdeth your deeds, and His Apostle, and the Believers; and then ye shall be brought back to the Knower of the hidden and the manifest(alike), then will He inform you of (all) what ye were doing.\nوَاٰخَرُوْنَ مُرْجَوْنَ لِاَمْرِ اللّٰهِ اِمَّا يُعَذِّبُهُمْ وَاِمَّا يَتُوْبُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(106)\nWA AAKHAROONA MURJAWNA LE-AMRE LAAHE IMMAA YUA’AZZEBUHUM WA AMMAA YATOOBU WA WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd others are made to await God’s command; whether He will chastise them or whether He will turn (in mercy)’, unto them And God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مَسْجِدًا ضِرَارًا وَّكُفْرًا وَّتَفْرِيْقًۢا بَيْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَاِرْصَادًا لِّمَنْ حَارَبَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَلَيَحْلِفُنَّ اِنْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اِلَّا الْحُسْنٰىؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَشْهَدُ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(107)\nWAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MASJEDAN ZERAARAL WWAKUFRAN WWATAFREEQAN BAYNA MOAMENEEN WAARSAADAN LEMAN HAARABA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU MIN QABL WA WALAYAHLEFUNNA IN AARADNAA ILLAA HUSNAA WAL LAAHO YASHHADO INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nAnd those who built a mosque to cause harm (to the faithful) and cause infidelity and to effect disunion among the faithful, and an ambush to him who warred against God and His Apostle before; and they will indeed swear (saying); “We only desired naught but good;” And God beareth witness that verily they are liars.\nلَا تَقُمْ فِيْهِ اَبَدًا ؕ لَمَسْجِدٌ اُسِّسَ عَلَى التَّقْوٰى مِنْ اَوَّلِ يَوْمٍ اَحَقُّ اَنْ تَقُوْمَ فِيْهِؕ فِيْهِ رِجَالٌ يُّحِبُّوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُطَّهِّرِيْنَ‏(108)\nLAA TAQUM FEEHE ABADAM LAMASJEDUN AUSSESA A’LAL TAQWAA MIN AAWLE YAWMIN AHAQQO AN TAQOOMA FEEH FEEHE REJAALUN YYUHEBBOONA AN YYATATAHHAROOA WAL LAAHO YOHIBBUL AL-MUTTAHHEREENA.\nNever do thou (O’ Apostle!) stand therein (to pray); Surely a mosque found on piety from the very first day deserveth more than thou shouldst stand therein (for prayers); therein are men who love that they be purified; And God loveth the purified ones.\nاَفَمَنْ اَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهٗ عَلٰى تَقْوٰى مِنَ اللّٰهِ وَرِضْوَانٍ خَيْرٌ اَمْ مَّنْ اَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهٗ عَلٰى شَفَا جُرُفٍ هَارٍ فَانْهَارَ بِهٖ فِىْ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(109)\nAFAMAWN AASSASA BUNYAANAH A’LAA TAQWAA MENAL LAAHE WAREZWAANIN KHAYRUL AM MAN AASSASA BUNYAANAH A’LAA SHAFAA JURUFIN HAARIN FAANHAARA BEHI FEE NAARE JAHANNAM WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nIs he therefore better who hath laid his foundation on fear of God and (His) goodwill, or he who layeth his foundation on the brink of a crumbling hollowed bank, so it crumbled down with him into the fire of Hell; and God guideth not people (who are) unjust.\nلَا يَزَالُ بُنْيَانُهُمُ الَّذِىْ بَنَوْا رِيْبَةً فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَقَطَّعَ قُلُوْبُهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(110)\nLAA YAZAALU BUNYAANUHUMU LAZEE BANAWA REEBATAN FEE QOLOOBEHIM ILLAA AN TAQATTAA’A QOLOOBOHUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nThe building which they built will not cease to be a source of disquiet in their hearts until their hearts are cut into pieces; and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ اشْتَرٰى مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَاَمْوَالَهُمْ بِاَنَّ لَهُمُ الْجَنَّةَ ؕ يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَيَقْتُلُوْنَ وَ يُقْتَلُوْنَوَعْدًا عَلَيْهِ حَقًّا فِى التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَالْاِنْجِيْلِ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ ؕ وَمَنْ اَوْفٰى بِعَهْدِهٖ مِنَ اللّٰهِ فَاسْتَبْشِرُوْا بِبَيْعِكُمُ الَّذِىْ بَايَعْتُمْ بِهٖ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(111)\nINNAL LAAHA ASHTARAA MENAL MOAMENEEN ANFOSAHUM WA AMWAALAHUM BE-ANNAL LAHOMUL JANNATA YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FAYAQTULOONA WA YUQTALOONAWAA’DAN A’LAYHE HAQQAN FIL WA WA INJEELE WAL QURAANIL WA MAN AWFAA BEA’AHDEH MENAL LAAHE FAASTABSHEROOA BEBAYE’EKUMU LAZEE BAAYAA’TUM BEHI WAZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nVerily God hath purchased from the faithful their selves and their properties, for theirs (in return) be the Garden (of Paradise); They fight in God’s way, and they slay and they are slain; (this is) a promise binding on Him in the ‘Torah ’ and the Evangel and the Qur’an; And who is (there) more faithful to his covenant than God? Therefore rejoice ye in the bargain that ye have transacted; and that, it is the great achievement.\nاَلتَّاۤئِبُوْنَ الْعٰبِدُوْنَ الْحٰمِدُوْنَ السّاۤئِحُوْنَ الرّٰكِعُوْنَ السّٰجِدُوْنَ الْاٰمِرُوْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَالنَّاهُوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَالْحٰفِظُوْنَ لِحُدُوْدِ اللّٰه ِؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nAALTTAAEBOONA AL-A’AABEDOONA AL-HAAMEDOONA AS-SAEHOONA AR-RAAKEU’OONA AS-SAAJEDOONA AL-AAAMEROONA BIL-MA’ROOF WAALNNAAHOONA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WAL HAAFEZOONA LEHUDOODE AL-LAAH WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\n(These are) They who turn unto God (seeking forgiveness), who worship (Him) who praise (Him) Who fast, who bow down, who prostrate themselves (in prayers) who enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil and keep (themselves) in God’s (ordained) limits; wherefore proclaim thou (O’ Our Apostle!) the glad tidings unto the believers.\nمَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِىِّ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْاۤ اَنْ يَّسْتَغْفِرُوْا لِلْمُشْرِكِيْنَ وَ لَوْ كَانُوْۤا اُولِىْ قُرْبٰى مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ اَنَّهُمْ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(113)\nMAA KAANA MOAMENATAN INW WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AN YYASTAGHFEROOA LIL-MUSHREKEENA WA LAW KAANOO OOLEE QURBAA MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHUM ANNAHUM ASHAABUN JAHEEM.\nIt is not for the Apostle and those who believe to seek forgiveness for the idolaters, even though they may be near of kin (to them) after it hath been declared (clearly) unto them that they are the inmates of the (flaming) Hell (fire).\nوَمَا كَانَ اسْتِغْفَارُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لِاَبِيْهِ اِلَّا عَنْ مَّوْعِدَةٍ وَّعَدَهَاۤ اِيَّاهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهٗۤ اَنَّهٗ عَدُوٌّ لِّلّٰهِ تَبَرَّاَ مِنْهُ ؕ اِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَاَوَّاهٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(114)\nWA MAA KAANA ASTEGHFAARU IBRAAHEEMA LEAABEEHE ILLAA A’N MMAWE’EDATIN WWAA’ADAHAA IYYAAHO FALAMMAA TABAYYANA LAHU ANNAHU A’DUWWUM LILLAAHE TABARRA-AL MINHO INNAL IBRAAHEEMA LAAWWAAHUN HALEEM.\nNor was Abraham’s seeking forgiveness for his father otherwise than due to a promise which he hath made unto him; but when it became clear unto him that he was an enemy unto God, he declared himself clear of him; verily Abraham was very tender-hearted, forbearing.\nوَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُضِلَّ قَوْمًۢا بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدٰٮهُمْ حَتّٰى يُبَيِّنَ لَهُمْ مَّا يَتَّقُوْنَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(115)\nWA MAA KAANA LAAHO LEEZELLA QAWMAN BA’DA IZ HADAAHUM HATTAA YUBAYNA LAHUM MAA YATTAQOONA INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nNor is it God to lead a people astray after He hath guided them (aright), He even maketh it clear unto them what they should abstain from; verily God knoweth all things.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(116)\nINNAL LAAHA LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ YOHYEE WA YOMEET WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nVerily God! His is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; He bringeth to life and He causeth to die; and there is not for you besides God any guardian or helper.\nلَقَدْ تَّابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَى النَّبِىِّ وَالْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ وَالْاَنْصَارِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْهُ فِىْ سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيْغُ قُلُوْبُ فَرِيْقٍ مِّنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْؕ اِنَّهٗ بِهِمْ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌۙ ‏(117)\nLAQAD TTAABA LAAHO A’LAL NESAAA-AN WA MOHAAJEREENAL WAL AANSAARE LAZEENA ATTABAU’OOHU FEE SAAA’ATE AL-U’USRATE MIN BA’DE MAA KAADA YAZEEGHU QULOOBU FAREEQIN MINHUM SUMMA TAABA WA INNAHU BEHIM RA-OOFUM RAHEEM.\nSurely hath turned God in mercy unto the Apostle, and the ‘Muhajirs ’ and the ‘Ansars ’ who followed him in the hour of distress after the hearts of a part of them had nearly swerved (from duty); but He turned unto them (also in mercy)’, Verily unto them He is Compassionate, Most Merciful.\nوَّعَلَى الثَّلٰثَةِ الَّذِيْنَ خُلِّفُوْا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ اَنْفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنْ لَّا مَلْجَاَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِلَّاۤ اِلَيْهِ ؕ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوْبُوْا  ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(118)\nWWAA’ALAA AS-SALAASATE LAZEENA KHULLEFOOA HATTAA EZAA ZAAQAT A’LAYHEMUL ARZO BEMAA RAHUBAT WAZAAQAT A’LAYHIM ANFOSOHUM WA ZANNOO AN LAA MALJAA MENAL LAAHE ILLAA ELAYHE SUMMA TAABA A’LAYHIM LE-YATOOBOO INNAL LAAHA HOWA TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nAnd on the three who were left behind; until the earth be-came straitened on them not withstanding its spaciousness and even their selves were also straitened on them that they thought that there was no refuge from God but unto Him; Then He turned unto them in mercy that they might turn (unto Him)’, Verily God, He is Oft-returning (to mercy), the Most Merciful.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَكُوْنُوْا مَعَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(119)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQUL LAAHA WA KOONOO LAAHA SAADEQEENA.\nO’ ye who believe! Fear ye God and be ye (always) with the Truthful ones.\nمَا كَانَ لِاَهْلِ الْمَدِيْنَةِ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَعْرَابِ اَنْ يَّتَخَلَّفُوْا عَنْ رَّسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَ لَا يَرْغَبُوْا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ لَا يُصِيْبُهُمْ ظَمَاٌ وَّلَا نَصَبٌ وَّلَا مَخْمَصَةٌ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا يَطَئُوْنَ مَوْطِئًا يَّغِيْظُ الْكُفَّارَ وَلَا يَنَالُوْنَ مِنْ عَدُوٍّ نَّيْلاً اِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُمْ بِهٖ عَمَلٌ صَالِحٌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَۙ‏(120)\nMAA KAANA LE-AHLIL MADEENATE WA MAN HAWLAHUM MENAL A-A’RAABE AN YYATAKHALLAFOOA A’N RRASOOLE LAAHE WA LAA YARGHABOOA BE-ANFOSEHIM A’N NNAFSEH ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM LAA YUSEEBUHUM ZAMAA WA LAA NASABUN WA LAA MAKHMASATUN FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAA YATAOONA MAWTEAN YYAGHEEZU KUFFAARA WA LAA YANAALOONA MIN A’ADOO NNAYLAAN ILLAA KOTEBA LAHUM BEHI A’AMALUN SAALEHUN INNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nIt was not for the people of Madina and those around them of the dwellers of the desert to stay away behind the Apostle of God, and nor to prefer their lives to his life; This is because there afflicteth them not thirst neither fatigue nor hunger in God’s way, nor tread they a path which enrages the infidels, nor do they receive from the enemy (any injury) but on account of it hath been reckoned to their credit a deed of righteousness; Verily God suffereth not to go in vain, the reward of the doers of good.\nوَلَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ نَفَقَةً صَغِيْرَةً وَّلَا كَبِيْرَةً وَّلَا يَقْطَعُوْنَ وَادِيًا اِلَّا كُتِبَ لَهُمْ لِيَجْزِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(121)\nWA LAA YUNFEQOONA NAFAQATAN SAGHEERATAN WA LAA KABEERATAN WA LAA YAQTAU’OONA WAADEEA ILLAA KOTEBA LAHUM LEEJZEEHUMU LAAHO AHSANAL MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nNor spend they anything (in the way of God), small or great, nor cut they across a valley, but it is recorded to their credit, that God may reward them with better than what they have been doing.\nوَمَا كَانَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ لِيَنْفِرُوْا كَآفَّةً ؕ فَلَوْلَا نَفَرَ مِنْ كُلِّ فِرْقَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ طَآئِفَةٌ لِّيَتَفَقَّهُوْا فِى الدِّيْنِ وَ لِيُنْذِرُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ اِذَا رَجَعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(122)\nWA MAA KAANA MOAMENOONA LEENFEROOA KAAAF-FATANW FA-LAWLAA NAFARA MIN KULLE FERQATIN MINHUM TAAEFATUN LLEETAFAQQAHOOA FIL DEENE WA LEENZEROOA QAWMAHUM EZAA RAJAU’OOA ELAYHIM LA-A’LLAHUM YAHZAROON.\nAnd nor is it for the faithful that they should go forth (to war) all together; why should not then a company from every party of them go forth that they may acquire (proper) understanding in religion, and that they may warn their people when they return unto them, so that they may be cautious?\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قَاتِلُوا الَّذِيْنَ يَلُوْنَكُمْ مِّنَ الْكُفَّارِ وَلْيَجِدُوْا فِيْكُمْ غِلْظَةً  ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْاۤ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(123)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO QAATELOOA LAZEENA YALOONAKUM MENAL KUFFAARE WALYAJEDOOA FEEKUM GHELZATAN WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nO’ ye who believe! Fight ye those of the infidels near to you and let them find in you firmness; and know ye that God is with those who guard (themselves) (against evil).\nوَاِذَا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ اَيُّكُمْ زَادَتْهُ هٰذِهٖۤ اِيْمَانًا ۚ فَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فَزَادَتْهُمْ اِيْمَانًا وَّهُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(124)\nWA EZAA MAA UNZELAT SOORATUN FA-MINHUM MAN YAQOOLO AYYOKUM ZAADATHU HAAZEHI EEMAANAW FA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO FAZAADATHUM EEMAANAW WA HUM YASTABSHEROON.\nAnd whenever a ‘Sura ’ is sent down, there are some of them (the hypocrites) who ask (one another) “which of you, hath this increased in faith?” But as for those who believe, it strengtheneth them in faith and they rejoice (at it).\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ فَزَادَتْهُمْ رِجْسًا اِلٰى رِجْسِهِمْ وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(125)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN FAZAADATHUM REJSAN ELAA REJSEHEM WA MAATOO WA HUM KAAFEROON.\nBut as to those in whose hearts is a disease it addeth unto them, uncleanliness to their uncleanliness and they shall die while they are infidels.\nاَوَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ يُفْتَنُوْنَ فِىْ كُلِّ عَامٍ مَّرَّةً اَوْ مَرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ لَا يَتُوْبُوْنَ وَلَا هُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(126)\nAWA LAA YARAWNAL ANNAHUM LAA YUFTANOON FEE KULLE FAN-ZUR MMARRATAN AW MARRATAYNE SUMMA LAA YATOOBOONA WA LAA HUM YAZZAKKAROONA.\nSee they not that they arc tried once or twice in every year and yet turn they not (unto God) and, and nor do they remember.\nوَاِذَا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَتْ سُوْرَةٌ نَّظَرَ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍؕ هَلْ يَرٰٮكُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ ثُمَّ انْصَرَفُوْا ؕ صَرَفَ اللّٰهُ قُلُوْبَهُمْ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(127)\nWA EZAA MAA UNZELAT SOORATUN NNAZARA KHALAA ELAA BA’Z WA HAL YARAAKUM MIN AHADIM SUMMA ANSARAFOOA SARAFA LAAHO QULOOBAHUM BE-ANNAHUM QAWMUN LAA YAFQAHOON.\nAnd whenever a ‘Sura’ is sent down, they cast glances at one another; (saying) “Doth he (the believer) seeth of you anyone?” Then they turn away; God hath turned away their hearts because they are a people who understand not.\nلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ عَزِيْزٌ عَلَيْهِ مَا عَنِتُّمْ حَرِيْصٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(128)\nLAQAD JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUM MIN ANFOSEKUM A’ZEEZUN A’LAYHE MAA A’ANETTUM HAREESUN A’LAYKUM BIL-MOAMENEENA RA-OOFUM RAHEEM.\nIndeed hath come unto you an Apostle from among your selves; grievous to him is your falling into distress, (he is) solicitous regarding your welfare, towards the faithful (he is) compassionate, (and) merciful.\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُلْ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ ۖ  لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ ؕ وَهُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(129)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FA-QUL HASBEYAL LAAH, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTO WA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL A’ZEEM. (129)\nBut if they turn away, Say thou: “Sufficeth me God; There is no god but He; On Him do I rely, and He is the Lord of the great ‘Arsh’ (i.e. the Glorious Throne of Mighty Power).",
  "merits": "This Surah has 129 verses and was revealed in Madinah. This Surah was revealed all at once and its revelation was accompanied by seventy thousand angels. It is narrated that keeping this Surah over one’s head (like in a cap or Amama) is a safety from thieves and destruction of property by fire. Also, keeping this Surah in one’s possession ensures safety from the evil designs of enemies."
